      "local_label": "Section 2.1 — Model (1)–(2)",
      "source_heading": "Section 2.1 — Model (1)–(2)",
      "source_kind": "source_passage",
      "statement_original": "Suppose we are given noisy data of the form\n\\[\nX_t=\\mu_t+Z_t,\\qquad t=1,\\ldots,n,\\tag{1}\n\\]\nwhere $\\mu_t$ are means or signals and $(Z_t)_{t\\in\\mathbb Z}$ is a stationary process with mean $0$, auto-covariance function $\\gamma(k)=\\operatorname{Cov}(Z_{t+k},Z_t)$, and finite long-run variance\n\\[\n0<\\sigma_\\infty^2:=\\sum_{k=-\\infty}^{\\infty}\\gamma(k)<\\infty.\\tag{2}\n\\]",
      "relation": "exact",
      "depends_on": [
        "D2"
      ],
      "evidence": [
