      "local_id": "D7",
      "local_label": "Section 2.3.1 — Block means (6)",
      "source_heading": "Section 2.3.1 — Block means (6)",
      "source_kind": "definition",
      "statement_original": "To reduce the noise from the data and to focus our attention on the signal, we will, here and in the following sections, split the data set into $m:=\\lfloor n/k\\rfloor$ blocks of size $k$ where $k\\to\\infty$ and $k/n\\to0$. Then we calculate the blocks’ sample means as follows:\n\\[\nR_j:=\\frac1k\\sum_{i=(j-1)k+1}^{jk}X_i,\\qquad j=1,2,\\ldots,m.\\tag{6}\n\\]",
      "relation": "exact",
      "depends_on": [
        "D1"
