    {
      "paper_id": "aos-2024-v52-i06-p2913",
      "local_id": "D19",
      "local_label": "Section 3.1 — Causal process (13)",
      "source_heading": "Section 3.1 — Causal process (13)",
      "source_kind": "source_passage",
      "statement_original": "In this framework, we view the causal stationary process $(Z_t)_{t\\in\\mathbb Z}$ as outputs from a physical system as follows\n\\[\nZ_t=G(\\ldots,\\varepsilon_{t-1},\\varepsilon_t),\\tag{13}\n\\]\nwhere $(\\varepsilon_t)_{t\\in\\mathbb Z}$, i. i. d., is the input information of this system and $G$ is an $\\mathbb R$-valued measurable function that can be thought of as a filter or, intuitively, “mechanism” of this system.",
      "relation": "exact",
      "depends_on": [],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 6,
          "location": "Section 3.1 — Causal process (13)"
        }
      ],
      "highlight_symbols": [
