    },
    {
      "paper_id": "aos-2024-v52-i06-p2913",
      "local_id": "D20",
      "local_label": "Section 3.1 — Functional dependence (14)",
      "source_heading": "Section 3.1 — Functional dependence (14)",
      "source_kind": "definition",
      "statement_original": "Then with this system, we measure the dependence from how much the outputs of this system will change if we replace the input information at time $t=0$ with an i. i. d. copy $\\varepsilon'_0$. Assume $\\mathbb E|Z_i|^\\theta<\\infty$, $\\theta\\ge1$. For a single observation at time $i$, we define the functional dependence measure as follows:\n\\[\n\\delta_{i,\\theta}=(\\mathbb E|Z_i-Z_{i,\\{0\\}}|^\\theta)^{1/\\theta},\\qquad\\text{where }Z_{i,\\{0\\}}=G(\\ldots,\\varepsilon_{-1},\\varepsilon'_0,\\varepsilon_1,\\ldots,\\varepsilon_i).\\tag{14}\n\\]",
      "relation": "exact",
      "depends_on": [
        "D19"
      ],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 7,
          "location": "Section 3.1 — Functional dependence (14)"
        }
      ],
      "highlight_symbols": [
